# unit-watch-remove.vrs: unit-watch D24 (Session 1), two tries, the removal and the next wave in game. uw-wave at the mark
# uw-a: Chaos kills three of wave 1's four spiders with `.devkill` (max 3), so one is left, and goes 150 m away;
# `.nyar event unstick uw-wave` marks the lone spider ("admin"). A3: the game's height correction lifts a unit sunk by
# `.devstrand under` back to its level within a frame, so the off-ground mark cannot be made in game; the off-ground rule
# itself is D3's unit test. An admin mark clears only by a fight, so with Chaos away each try fails StuckSeconds (90 s)
# after its move: "recovered: … try 1/2", "try failed: … try 1/2 (still stuck)", then try 2 (a second move, or with Chaos
# within 100 m of a player landing "try failed: … try 2/2 (seen)") and "removed: … after 2 tries, no kill credit"; wave 1 is then cleared by the removal's staged
# despawn and "event uw-wave wave 2/2" follows within 10 s of it; `event info` shows "1 removed"; the admin stop's
# scoreboard holds Chaos's three `.devkill` kills only, one fewer than wave 1's count.
#
# Needs: what unit-watch.vrs needs (StallMinutes 10: a 1-minute backstop would mark the lone spider first).
# Run: --var AX=-1880 --var AZ=-1640 --var FX=-1730 --var FZ=-1640
ensure
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
console TPHome
wait 3
chat .nyar event reload
expect-log events: reloaded
chat .devtp ${AX} ${AZ}
expect-log \[DEV TP\] to x=(?P<PX>-?[0-9.]+) y=-?[0-9.]+ z=(?P<PZ>-?[0-9.]+)
wait 4
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
chat .devmark uw-a
expect-log \[DEV MARK\] uw-a
chat .nyar event set uw-wave location here
expect-reply uw-wave action.location =
mark
chat .nyar event start uw-wave
expect-log event uw-wave started by manual timeout=20
expect-log event uw-wave wave 1/2 timeout=30
wait 8
chat .devkill -581295882 40 3
expect-log \[DEV KILL\] n=3
# Chaos 150 m away, then the lone spider marked by `.nyar event unstick` (A3: a sunk unit does not stay sunk)
chat .devtp ${FX} ${FZ}
expect-log \[DEV TP\] to
wait 4
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
chat .nyar event unstick uw-wave
expect-reply unstick uw-wave: 1 units marked, 0 fighting left alone
expect-log \[nyar\] unit-watch uw-wave stuck: CHAR_Spider_Forest wave 1 \(admin\) timeout=10
expect-log \[nyar\] unit-watch uw-wave recovered: CHAR_Spider_Forest try 1/2, [0-9]+ m \((group|player|anchor)\) timeout=10
chat .nyar event info uw-wave
expect-reply unit watch: 1 stuck now, 1 recovered, 0 removed
# no fight within StuckSeconds after the move: an admin mark's try fails, then the second try, then the removal
expect-log \[nyar\] unit-watch uw-wave try failed: CHAR_Spider_Forest try 1/2 \(still stuck\) timeout=100
# try 1 lands it 50-60 m from Chaos (a player landing), so try 2 sees a player within 100 m: it waits, fails "(seen)" after
# StuckSeconds, and the removal waits at most StuckSeconds more, then goes ahead even in view (D6, S-10); a group or
# anchor landing out of view gives a second move instead
expect-log \[nyar\] unit-watch uw-wave (recovered: CHAR_Spider_Forest try 2/2, [0-9]+ m|try failed: CHAR_Spider_Forest try 2/2 \(seen\)) timeout=100
expect-log \[nyar\] unit-watch uw-wave removed: CHAR_Spider_Forest wave 1 after 2 tries, no kill credit timeout=200
# the removal cleared wave 1: the next wave comes
expect-log event uw-wave wave 1 cleared timeout=10
expect-log event uw-wave wave 2/2 timeout=10
chat .nyar event info uw-wave
expect-reply 1 removed
shot full uw-removed-info
# the scoreboard: Chaos's three kills, no credit for the removal
chat .nyar event stop uw-wave
expect-log event uw-wave stopped
expect-log event uw-wave scoreboard: 1 players, 3 kills, 0 deaths
expect-chat scoreboard: 1. Chaos 3 kills timeout=20
shot full uw-scoreboard
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units: 0 timeout=40
console TPHome
wait 3
